{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-127499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/2f08e0a0d1fd855f2d179ac65dbdf5d022f3488b85c78b5cbb507f12bd69487e.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our circle is centered at $(-1,1)$ and has a radius of $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-(-1))^{2}+(y-1)^{2}={1}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+1)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y-1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)+2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{y-1} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x+1}{1-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127499" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127499" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+1)(1-y)"] ["math" "2(x+1)(y+1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1-x}{y+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{2(x+1)}{y-1}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+1}{1-y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127499" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x+1}{1-y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/78ad1a6835bb71441f77a3ca2bbdc93a42635e0386cda35fbe5fc9b0c9f48677.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our circle is centered at $(-3,-2)$ and has a radius of $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-(-3))^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2}={2}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x+3)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+3)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+3)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+2)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+3)+2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+3}{y+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2(y+2)}{x+3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{x+3}{y+2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2(x-3)}{y-2}"] ["math" "\\frac{y+2}{x+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{y+2}{x-3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{x+3}{y+2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/812f88e913650b7924fc13acc7adde999819d0011fa547a7e0ad73cb37e3939f.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our circle is centered at $(0,-2)$ and has a radius of $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-0)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2}={3}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+2)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{x+2}{3y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{x}{y+2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{y+2}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{y+2}"] ["math" "\\frac{y}{x+2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{x}{y+2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/f24d078ca0dc57ebd12778b7862683b0289e9c0d4c664639bd210dcc1f7c6d1b.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our circle is centered at the origin and has a radius of $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={4}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(16) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{4x}{y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{x}{y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{2x}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{y}{x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{x}{y}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/a3ca092dc7c0668ac465d4832b91a2b831af057ff22e357b4e7105bfb454ea18.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our circle is centered at $(1,0)$ and has a radius of $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}+(y-0)^{2}={2}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-1)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(1-x)y"] ["math" "-(x+1)y"] ["math" "-\\frac{x+1}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{1-x}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+1}{y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1-x}{y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/c0295c7cdc1abc16273efda842a0aa7a892ece2f5dda5e29f7baab25320b23ec.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $1$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2x}{y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4x}{y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{y}{2x}"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{4y}"] ["math" "\\frac{y}{4x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4x}{y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/f8effaf21270245ed6f8df63d2e430483756f47537b1c7325e88acc5286544db.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $2$ and $5,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2y}{25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{25x}{4y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{25x}{4y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5x}{2y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5y}{2x}"] ["math" "\\frac{25y}{4x}"] ["math" "\\frac{5x}{2y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{25x}{4y}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/547b79b566d2914db4a63997cd5fc9f02dd1517b8dcd5e53cde8c07ac5ca05a2.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $3$ and $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{9}+2y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{9y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3y}{x}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9x}{y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9y}{x}"] ["math" "-\\frac{x}{3y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{x}{9y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{x}{9y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/e4c39b409f6049a4fdead506c329d232820876c37ede9540adfeade2d7c1b9dc.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our ellipse is centered at $(3,0)$ and has semiaxes $3$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x-3)}{9}+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2(x-3)}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3y}{2(x-3)}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4(y-3)}{9x}"] ["math" "\\frac{2(x-3)}{3y}"] ["math" "\\frac{9x}{4(y-3)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/43e8ed1ee117ccd10f0e3aa03fc8db8ec1db6c076689e9072e1e22e048dfc279.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $5$ and $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{25}+\\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x}{25} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{9x}{25y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127512" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127512" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3x}{5y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9x}{25y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9y}{25x}"] ["math" "\\frac{25y}{9x}"] ["math" "\\frac{5y}{3x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127512" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{9x}{25y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-312780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/b269001ff5a3a1a1d86125157ee2f5b77d89ebcf0041f8d403dbc931b796c5e8.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-312780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(5,7).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5$ and $y=7$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(7)^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\ 49 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{49}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\frac{49}{5}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{49}{5}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{10y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-312780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-312780" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-312780" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{49}{10y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/c403f11093b76facafbecb72bcc413640ac67fe6ed73d6b64374230f39e29aba.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-3,-1).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-3$ and $y=-1$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2} & =4p(-3) \\\\ 1 & =-12p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{6y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-342215" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342215" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{6y}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/5eedb15e515993bdc8a2ee37ab4c7c0e0225b9d2118d5d60e8593de5ea56f199.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-1,2).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ and $y=2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =4p(-1) \\\\ 4 & =-4p \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-4x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-127515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2y}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-127515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/85d75e0f3a9f2a30282d1f1754b0c46da49e8f73ff2a858c856ba5492eb21cca.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(8,-8).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=8$ and $y=-8$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=8x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-342354" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342354" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{y}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/7367cb4ae1feb4e18b98b712687ceb4a1db67f8c9e4965af3ffd1253a827f346.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-6,6).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-6$ and $y=6$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 36 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-6x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-6x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-6 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{3}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e74e14fe59fc1496ba7117540ba4f6ffaf12694a7a28b279bfb0eef03a709"} {"question" "q-342218" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "q-342218" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/state.json" "file_sha256" "049cf949a5e3bb4d727c674b0e85a519fc509ae6e2ae447c16ab12a4f04226e0"} {"question" "e-9577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/0f4f0de23892a6f76642f8c7e5d3a6112a8ffa2d9f50000cd974f293a7d8b3b6.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/example-9577.json" "file_sha256" "989fe994749b92a4c40731e8508ab9e7c14c6570692d5a84aa2bbc398e45b2e9"} {"question" "e-9577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our circle is centered at $(0,-1)$ and has a radius of $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-0)^2 + (y - (-1))^2 = 2^2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx^2 + (y+1)^2 = 4.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2(y+1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/example-9577.json" "file_sha256" "989fe994749b92a4c40731e8508ab9e7c14c6570692d5a84aa2bbc398e45b2e9"} {"question" "e-9578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/d3895bafe045f7e460887aee41bf390fdda753fed87eaab14f4a29ddb792267c.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/example-9578.json" "file_sha256" "ce193a5b97b414a78cd2245e0b50c216d3534536d85bca7589fdb3164b78f68b"} {"question" "e-9578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $2$ and $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{2^2} + \\dfrac{y^2}{4^2} = 1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad \\dfrac{x^2}{4} + \\dfrac{y^2}{16} = 1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2y}{16}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{y}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/example-9578.json" "file_sha256" "ce193a5b97b414a78cd2245e0b50c216d3534536d85bca7589fdb3164b78f68b"} {"question" "e-9579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/a92eae1ab0af29ea895b570c95199ece1e292c09953ebb2dabbb7c6e2d422d6c.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/example-9579.json" "file_sha256" "7b1999b7aaabff74cdaa3e09e9456f79f85e592f5fdc44cfb7819948c96a70ee"} {"question" "e-9579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(3,-2).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\ny^2 = 4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x = 3$ and $y = -2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 4 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\ny^2 = \\dfrac{4}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{3y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/example-9579.json" "file_sha256" "7b1999b7aaabff74cdaa3e09e9456f79f85e592f5fdc44cfb7819948c96a70ee"}] "usage" {"e-9578" [] "e-9577" [] "e-9579" []} "basis" 2025 "retractions" [[17592186166650 :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the circle shown above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3216/Source/Images/ed62e909ea502542ef307e57c0edb2a4.png)"] [17592186166650 :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(0,-1)$ and has a radius of $2$, its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-0)^2 + (y - (-1))^2 = 2^2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x^2 + (y+1)^2 = 4\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}\n$$\n\nwe use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2} + (y + 1)^{2}) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(4) \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2}) + \\frac{d}{dx}((y + 1)^{2}) &= 0 \\\\\n2x + 2(y + 1)\\frac{dy}{dx} &= 0 \\\\\n2(y + 1)\\frac{dy}{dx} &= -2x \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= -\\frac{x}{y + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186166651 :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3216/Source/Images/fa26d004a0d7f5f86a31ea3f8071a534.png)"] [17592186166651 :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $2$ and $4$, its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{2^2} + \\dfrac{y^2}{4^2} = 1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad \\dfrac{x^2}{4} + \\dfrac{y^2}{16} = 1\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}\n$$\n\nwe use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \\frac{y^{2}}{16}) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(1) \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{x^{2}}{4}) + \\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{y^{2}}{16}) &= 0 \\\\\n\\frac{2x}{4} + \\frac{2y}{16} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} &= 0 \\\\\n\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{y}{8} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} &= 0 \\\\\n\\frac{y}{8} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} &= -\\frac{x}{2} \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= -\\frac{4x}{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186166652 :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3216/Source/Images/6dfd6abbaf5d73a917c476962cd3cecf.png)"] [17592186166652 :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O$, and passes through the point $(3,-2)$.\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\ny^2 = 4px\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x = 3$ and $y = -2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-2)^{2} &= 4p(3) \\\\\n4 &= 12p \\\\\np &= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is\n\n$$\ny^2 = \\dfrac{4}{3}x\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}\n$$\n\nwe use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(y^{2}) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{4}{3}x) \\\\\n2y\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{4}{3} \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{2}{3y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
